6;eATxMCs6eWsg-oQ-2gOEmtcEXNPra3SEHoJoFOiFjGQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx2026-07-23T22:08:03.088Zƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;yflHO9Mvd6ujy6J6g7OXy3a4zxNIUYZF4DRIakGg2JEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxyhttps://theconversation.com/the-commonwealth-games-are-here-with-fewer-sports-more-nations-and-an-uncertain-future-287484ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-uv3tI9rMQ8rsHeY2vS3aN6rLrMOJcGw6YpcIy9Z92Iƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9https://newscable-source-broker.invalid/activitypub/actorƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0RmbUNKOdgZgO7iKzMe1rm3dbI-SO_2UpKYmSL65qRAƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;65EbDn2E3b6Q3DuA8wDm0pGYwZU1Tq0LQV21K8HUh7sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxyhttps://theconversation.com/the-commonwealth-games-are-here-with-fewer-sports-more-nations-and-an-uncertain-future-287484ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AOcc2ZJ413n1B2MlhdZhHvmVeglSVf0DzbM3CT0oA7Aƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky8Ÿ<p>Victoria was supposed to be gearing up to welcome athletes from around the world for the 2026 Commonwealth Games. Instead, the competition is getting underway in <a href="https://www.glasgow2026.com/welcometoglasgow">Glasgow</a>, Scotland. </p> <p>The 2026 event was <a href="https://www.olympics.com/en/news/australia-s-victoria-to-host-2026-commonwealth-games">originally</a> awarded to Victoria. However, the state withdrew in July 2023 because of <a href="https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-07-18/victoria-commonwealth-games-announcement-daniel-andrews/102613156">increasing costs</a>. </p> <p>It was feared this decision could lead to the games becoming <a href="https://www.heraldsun.com.au/sport/commonwealth-games/glasgow-confirmed-as-hosts-as-2026-commonwealth-games-are-saved-with-aussie-help/news-story/9f3b71e99fe047829dc2dff2e39f5196">extinct</a>.</p> <p>However, after discussions with numerous different cities, Glasgow was <a href="https://www.commonwealthsport.com/news/4153255/glasgow-confirmed-as-2026-commonwealth-games-hosts">confirmed</a> as the replacement <a href="https://www.espn.com.au/olympics/story/_/id/41919855/2026-commonwealth-games-glasgow-confirmed-host-city">host city</a> in September 2024.</p> <p></p> <p>So, what does this yearâ€™s event look like, who are the Australians to watch and what does the future hold for the games?</p> <h2>What are the Commonwealth Games?</h2> <p>Similar to the Olympics, the <a href="https://www.commonwealthsport.com/commonwealth-games">Commonwealth Games</a> is a long-standing international sports event held every four years, except for cancellations during <a href="https://www.sbs.com.au/sport/article/miracle-miles-and-political-protests-a-brief-history-of-the-commonwealth-games/xb5t6r0xc">world wars</a>. </p> <p>In contrast to the Olympics, they are open only to countries within the <a href="https://www.historyextra.com/period/20th-century/commonwealth-games-history-facts-countries-sports/">Commonwealth of Nations</a>: predominantly English-speaking former colonies of the <a href="https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/sports-and-leisure/commonwealth-games">British Empire</a>. </p> <p>In fact, the games were called the British Empire Games when they began in <a href="https://www.commonwealthsport.com/commonwealth-games">1930</a>. </p> <figure> <iframe width="440" height="260" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/iqnH4K1seTs?wmode=transparent&amp;start=0" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen=""></iframe> <figcaption><span class="caption">Images from Empire Games In Sydney, 1938.</span></figcaption> </figure> <p>The title Commonwealth Games has only been used since <a href="https://www.olympics.com/en/news/commonwealth-games-first-edition-year-country-host">1978</a>. </p> <p>This year will be the <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/glasgow-to-welcome-commonwealth-in-2026">23rd Commonwealth Games</a>. Most previous editions have been <a href="https://www.commonwealthsport.com/nations/canada">hosted by larger Commonwealth countries</a> such as Australia (five times), Canada (four), England (four) and New Zealand (three). </p> <p>The Commonwealth nations represent a combined 2.5 billion people: nearly a <a href="https://thecommonwealth.org/our-member-countries">third</a> of the total world population. </p> <h2>A smaller event than usual</h2> <p>The Commonwealth Games has always had fewer sports and <a href="https://www.historyextra.com/period/20th-century/commonwealth-games-history-facts-countries-sports/">fewer</a> athletes than the Olympics. However, the 2026 event will be even smaller than usual.</p> <p>Glasgowâ€™s pitch for hosting the 2026 games consisted of a <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cj6nyp4zzzyo">scaled-down</a> version. </p> <p>The <a href="https://www.smh.com.au/sport/swimming/summer-bummer-mcintosh-to-skip-commonwealth-games-20250801-p5mjgg.html">Birmingham 2022</a> games included <a href="https://www.news.com.au/sport/commonwealth-games/what-new-sports-are-in-the-birmingham-commonwealth-games/news-story/2e1dd211c71118b9b8c0f9d028bb7ef9">20</a> <a href="https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-07-28/biggest-international-names-birmingham-commonwealth-games/101197524">sports</a> and more than <a href="https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-07-28/biggest-international-names-birmingham-commonwealth-games/101197524">5,000</a> <a href="https://www.news.com.au/sport/commonwealth-games/what-new-sports-are-in-the-birmingham-commonwealth-games/news-story/2e1dd211c71118b9b8c0f9d028bb7ef9">athletes</a>. </p> <p>Glasgow 2026 will feature <a href="https://www.glasgow2026.com/news/4381372/ten-days-215-gold-medals-3-000-athletes-glasgow-2026-sport-schedule-released-">3,000</a> athletes competing in <a href="https://www.glasgow2026.com/sports">ten</a> sports. </p> <p>But the 2026 event will have the <a href="https://www.commonwealthsport.com/news/4211556/glasgow-2026-announces-largest-ever-para-sport-medal-event-programme">largest</a> integrated para sport program in Commonwealth Games history. Six of the ten sports will have a <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly3yv91595o">para</a> equivalent.</p> <p>The inclusion of Gabon and Togo also means a record <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cj6nyp4zzzyo">74 nations</a> will be contesting events. </p> <p>To <a href="https://www.espn.com.au/olympics/story/_/id/41933198/hockey-diving-cricket-sports-axed-2026-commonwealth-games">save money</a>, the ten sports will be spread across just <a href="https://www.glasgow2026.com/venues">four venues</a>, all within a 12 kilometre corridor in central Glasgow. </p> <p>Athletes and support staff will stay in <a href="https://www.skysports.com/more-sports/news/19884/13238591/commonwealth-games-2026-rugby-and-cricket-among-sports-dropped-from-scaled-down-event">hotel accommodation</a> rather than an athletesâ€™ village. The opening and closing ceremonies will also be <a href="https://www.sbs.com.au/news/article/from-hockey-to-diving-the-sports-being-cut-from-the-commonwealth-games/gvh3mdkpn">smaller</a>.</p> <p><iframe id="3H0wr" class="tc-infographic-datawrapper" src="https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/3H0wr/" height="400px" width="100%" style="border: 0;" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" title="Sports featured in the 2026 Commonwealth Games"></iframe></p> <p>Many of the omitted sports are <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly3yv91595o">team sports</a>, which greatly decreased the number of athletes, and associated costs such as transport and accommodation. </p> <p>Others such as aquatics, cycling and gymnastics are still included but have <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly3yv91595o">fewer events</a> (such as cycling, which no longer includes road cycling or mountain biking). </p> <p>Many sports are understandably <a href="https://www.sbs.com.au/news/article/from-hockey-to-diving-the-sports-being-cut-from-the-commonwealth-games/gvh3mdkpn">disappointed</a> to not be included, especially <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2024/oct/22/commonwealth-games-2026-schedule-scotland">rugby</a>, <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly3yv91595o">squash</a> and <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly3yv91595o">hockey</a>, whose governing bodies argue appropriate venues already exist in Glasgow. </p> <p>Officials have stated athletics and swimming will be the only <a href="https://www.bbc.com/sport/commonwealth-games/58870657">compulsory sports</a> at future Commonwealth Games. So, all the sports omitted for 2026 could be included again in <a href="https://www.skysports.com/more-sports/news/19884/13238591/commonwealth-games-2026-rugby-and-cricket-among-sports-dropped-from-scaled-down-event">future events</a>. </p> <h2>The Australians with an eye on gold</h2> <p>Australia boasts <a href="https://aapnews.aap.com.au/news/weightlifter-out-to-maintain-golden-games-haul">reigning</a> <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/six-reigning-champions-named-among-25-strong-cycling-team-for-glasgow-2026/">Commonwealth champions</a> and <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/australia-names-powerhouse-bowls-squad-for-glasgow-2026-commonwealth-games/">medal</a> <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/proven-medallists-and-rising-stars-headline-gymnastics-team-for-glasgow-2026/">chances</a> in nearly every sport on the 2026 program. </p> <p></p> <p>They should again be one of the <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/birmingham-2022-team-honoured-with-australian-sports-medal">teams</a> to beat after topping the Birmingham 2022 medal table with 67 golds. </p> <p>Direct comparisons and predictions are difficult, because Glasgow will have fewer sports and gold-medal <a href="https://www.glasgow2026.com/news/4381372/ten-days-215-gold-medals-3-000-athletes-glasgow-2026-sport-schedule-released">events</a>.</p> <p>Swimming <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/aye-dolphins-are-pure-dead-brilliant-australian-team-named-for-2026-commonwealth-games/">remains</a> Australiaâ€™s biggest gold mine. The 60-member Dolphins <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/aye-dolphins-are-pure-dead-brilliant-australian-team-named-for-2026-commonwealth-games/">team</a> will be <a href="https://www.swimming.org.au/articles/glas-glow-for-60-dolphins-australias-comm-games-team-named">headlined</a> by Mollie Oâ€™Callaghan, Cam McEvoy and Kyle Chalmers, alongside leading para swimmers such as <a href="https://www.swimming.org.au/articles/para-swimmers-named-for-2026-commonwealth-games">Tim Hodge</a> and <a href="https://www.swimmingworldmagazine.com/news/australia-names-18-strong-para-swim-team-for-2026-glasgow-commonwealth-games/">Lakeisha Patterson</a>. </p> <p>Australia won <a href="https://www.swimming.org.au/articles/dolphins-close-birmingham-2022-campaign">25 swimming golds</a> in Birmingham and has the depth to dominate again.</p> <p>Athletics also <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/australian-athletics-cohort-completes-glasgow-2026-team-puzzle/">offers</a> major chances. </p> <p>Olympic pole vault champion Nina Kennedy <a href="https://worldathletics.org/athletes/australia/nina-kennedy-1440759">returns</a> as the defending Commonwealth champion, as does <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/australian-athletics-cohort-completes-glasgow-2026-team-puzzle/?fbclid=IwY2xjawTFScNleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETFYb2V6OGhRYzZCRUVoTG1Ic3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHtVXKUJgn6I_iw-95dgToyV8fR_vwDFAc5AtNfQ2f7crYHXu6S7blzdiFR8E_aem_aVer4pGOiaGWhE8mNGNp8g">Kurtis Marshall</a> in the menâ€™s pole vault.</p> <p>Olympic silver medallist Jess Hull will <a href="https://worldathletics.org/athletes/australia/jessica-hull-14464506">contest</a> the mile and 5,000 metres, while Olympic bronze medallist and defending discus champion Matt Denny is another leading <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/australian-athletics-cohort-completes-glasgow-2026-team-puzzle/">prospect</a>. </p> <p>Other key athletics medal <a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/australian-athletics-cohort-completes-glasgow-2026-team-puzzle/?fbclid=IwY2xjawTFScNleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETFYb2V6OGhRYzZCRUVoTG1Ic3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHtVXKUJgn6I_iw-95dgToyV8fR_vwDFAc5AtNfQ2f7crYHXu6S7blzdiFR8E_aem_aVer4pGOiaGWhE8mNGNp8g">chances</a> include:</p> <ul> <li><p><a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/australian-athletics-cohort-completes-glasgow-2026-team-puzzle/?fbclid=IwY2xjawTFScNleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETFYb2V6OGhRYzZCRUVoTG1Ic3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHtVXKUJgn6I_iw-95dgToyV8fR_vwDFAc5AtNfQ2f7crYHXu6S7blzdiFR8E_aem_aVer4pGOiaGWhE8mNGNp8g">Cameron Myers</a> (1 mile)</p></li> <li><p><a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/athletes/eleanor-patterson/">Eleanor Patterson</a> (high jump)</p></li> <li><p><a href="https://commonwealthgames.com.au/athletes/jemima-montag/">Jemima Montag</a> (10,000m walk).</p></li> </ul> <p>The Diamonds are <a href="https://netball.sport/events-and-results/world-rankings-hub/current-world-rankings">ranked</a> number one in world netball and will defend their title, although New Zealand, England and Jamaica ensure gold is far from automatic.</p> <h2>What does the future hold?</h2> <p>Is public interest in the Commonwealth Games fading? The evidence is mixed. </p> <p>The host model is under pressure, as Victoriaâ€™s withdrawal and Glasgowâ€™s compact <a href="https://www.glasgow2026.com/news/4153255/glasgow-confirmed-as-2026-commonwealth-games-hosts">replacement</a> show. The eventâ€™s governing body, Commonwealth Sport, has responded with a â€œ<a href="https://www.commonwealthsport.com/commonwealth-sport/games-reset">Games Reset</a>â€ intended to make future events more flexible and relevant.</p> <p>They hope the smaller model can <a href="https://www.straitstimes.com/sport/glasgow-confirmed-as-host-city-for-2026-commonwealth-games">increase</a> the number of cities <a href="https://www.bbc.com/sport/commonwealth-games/58870657">willing</a> to <a href="https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/glasgow-2026s-leaner-model-inspires-future-hosts">host</a> future games.</p> <p>Audience interest has not disappeared in Australia. Channel Seven <a href="https://sevenwestmedia.com.au/assets/pdfs/Birmingham-2022-wins-gold-with-viewers.pdf">reported</a> Birmingham 2022 reached 11.1 million Australians on broadcast television â€“ equivalent to roughly two in five Australians â€“ and 2.15 million viewers used 7plus. </p> <p>This was substantial, but below the roughly 20 million Australians <a href="https://www.nineforbrands.com.au/media-release/19-5-million-australians-captivated-by-paris-2024/">reached</a> by the recent Tokyo and Paris Olympics.</p> <p>Organisers for the 2026 Commonwealth Games also reported strong Glasgow ticket demand, with the swimming pool and velodrome virtually <a href="https://www.commonwealthsport.com/news/4487767/100-days-to-go">sold out</a> three months before the event.</p> <p>Australiaâ€™s medal rush should attract viewers but the gamesâ€™ future will depend on affordable hosting, strong stories, inclusion and benefits that remain after the podiums are packed away.</p><img src="https://counter.theconversation.com/content/287484/count.gif" alt="The Conversation" width="1" height="1" /> <p class="fine-print"><em><span>The authors do not work for, consult, own shares in or receive funding from any company or organisation that would benefit from this article, and have disclosed no relevant affiliations beyond their academic appointment.</span></em></p>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;nDQ6Pgn1mr_R5JuzPoytn83IvGrXcYRGQ5x_GaitUJoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;hrWeq7EiCipI2rv8PWCRfwreU3-5I9kox2vS8snE4Icƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;GnEwbACK8Q2HqLx3pvBfyt85-zD0KB630EJR854E6bcƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;p1HbtgHriBTmmtBNc7DHPdBjsjXVZl34bZm0Ez91-VEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;a-R72o8EpEn0TOgfbHm2qeFjZqwtUVtp_Zuy50yNUN4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;nimWJIN3YbkAHVYwsTvcDSnM4C3P-YgdzDO0VtYZVGwƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WB-jQVYgtwlAZgBhONkiEPFCaXiVFo_2078jXUHx3eoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;_Lvxt2yd-GrsYd8PCAcft7EO-Um79rpWwVQyKBtUFOkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqSyndicationSourceƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KckmpQnx1nPgBn7DyG0-PzbX3uLEIQEun-te-65Ib08ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx(urn:rmn:predicate:source-reports-summaryƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;k1Ag3n4umTS8wqORkc3_hdZrX_06MN-Wa7c35ZGTJuQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarktUnsaturatedPredicateƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;17yV3WPdJ1ljfKYVvD7FnVH3s08RKKj7u6xDJlJwMtwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarksGroundedPredicationƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AURrFMD5-iGon4-gU0i6egB9mTooK6wQpsVZBDg1m04ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KX_u6-vN5dKWO5t7sFxqWP3NgT7Yv5A49jCuTOqX3ggƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;fMTricU4vA797uDStCevW9oa-D2kXM_jtkjVRI12qckƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx2026-07-23T22:08:03.088Zƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;3GZ9ZgTmBr0ZC-_1vAFOL3ov2ShVk3s6W3TyV4NF2VYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxyhttps://theconversation.com/the-commonwealth-games-are-here-with-fewer-sports-more-nations-and-an-uncertain-future-287484ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Aw4WsW15ramKxHPZz14tsKgq3o-kYl0Qh8eSEeNcxakƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9https://newscable-source-broker.invalid/activitypub/actorƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;z3DLNxhZxUBw63BjP6Em2Lt_dmbmpkCz8mZC5bBq2z4ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;fbgU9nQg6kyFaTsIN_xxS-K92FBhB1nfvxOMmw5gbLYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxyhttps://theconversation.com/the-commonwealth-games-are-here-with-fewer-sports-more-nations-and-an-uncertain-future-287484ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;QP74Uszwwnbd5bij5k2meNdn_oETzNns6VS2_2FRh0Eƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkt2026-07-22T23:55:28Zƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bZ1dYJIiHq5a6ZP